<title>USA: Signature Resorts Q1 shr rises.</title>
<headline>Signature Resorts Q1 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Signature Resorts, Inc. and Subsidiaries</p>
<p>			    Consolidated Statements of Income</p>
<p>			Three Months ended March 31, 1997 and 1996</p>
<p>					   (unaudited)</p>
<p>					March 31, 1997    March 31, 1996</p>
<p>						  Actual     Pro Forma (a)</p>
<p>Revenues:</p>
<p>	 Vacation Interval sales	  45,796		19,889</p>
<p>	 Interest income		     5,393		 2,489</p>
<p>	 Other income			  2,366		 1,729</p>
<p>	   Total revenue		   $53,555	     $24,107</p>
<p>Costs and operating expenses:</p>
<p>	 Merger related expenses	   1,693		    --</p>
<p>	 Vacation Intervals cost of sales</p>
<p>						  12,061		 5,021</p>
<p>	 Advertising, sales and marketing</p>
<p>						  20,760		 9,456</p>
<p>	 Loan Portfolio:</p>
<p>	 Interest expense - treasury     2,259		 1,534</p>
<p>	 Other				     488		   288</p>
<p>	 Provision for doubtful accounts 2,057		   717</p>
<p>	 General and administrative	7,031		 4,075</p>
<p>	 Depreciation and amortization   1,078		   601</p>
<p>	   Total Costs and operating expenses</p>
<p>						 $47,427	     $21,692</p>
<p>     Income from operations		6,128		 2,415</p>
<p>	 Interest expense - other	  2,384		   447</p>
<p>	 Capitalized interest		(494)		 (847)</p>
<p>	 Equity in loss (gain) in joint venture</p>
<p>						    (89)		   147</p>
<p>     Income before taxes		   4,327		 2,668</p>
<p>	 Provision for income taxes	1,731		 1,067</p>
<p>     Net income			     $2,596		$1,601</p>
<p>     Earnings per share		    $0.13		 $0.09</p>
<p>Weighted average common and common</p>
<p>equivalent shares outstanding</p>
<p>					    19,990,000	  18,275,000</p>
<p>NOTES: (a)  The pro forma statement of income gives effect to the consolidation of the company's predecessor corporations, partnerships, and limited liability companies and the company's initial public offering as if they had occurred at the beginning of the period ended March 31, 1996.</p>
<p>Reported net income of $2,596,000 and reported earnings per share of $0.13 differ from recurring net income and recurring earnings per share by $1,016,000 and $0.05, respectively, reflecting a one-time charge of $1,693,000 ($1,016,000, net of income taxes) incurred during the first quarter 1997 for merger expenses related to the acquisition of AVCOM International Inc.</p>
</text>
